{"name":"Healing Plant","hex":"#6c7d42","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"healing","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The process where the cells in the body regenerate and repair themselves.","An act of healing, as by a faith healer."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of heal"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/healing"},{"term":"plant","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An organism that is not an animal, especially an organism capable of photosynthesis, and typically a small or herbaceous organism of this kind, rather than a tree.","An organism of the kingdom Plantae, and now specifically, a living organism of the Embryophyta (land plants) or of the Chlorophyta (green algae), a eukaryote that includes double-membraned chloroplasts in its cells containing chlorophyll a and b, or any organism closely related to such an organism."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To place (a seed or plant) in soil or other substrate in order that it may live and grow.","To furnish or supply with plants."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plant"}],"entries":[{"title":"Healing","blocks":[{"text":"Regarding physical trauma or disease suffered by an organism, healing involves the repairing of damaged tissue(s), organs and the biological system as a whole and resumption of (normal) functioning. Medicine includes the process by which the cells in the body regenerate and repair to reduce the size of a damaged or necrotic area and replace it with new living tissue. The replacement can happen in two ways: by regeneration in which the necrotic cells are replaced by new cells that form \"like\" tissue as was originally there; or by repair in which injured tissue is replaced with scar tissue. Most organs will heal using a mixture of both mechanisms."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/417_Tissue_Repair.jpg/330px-417_Tissue_Repair.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Healing","wikidata":"Q1581290"},{"title":"Plant","blocks":[{"text":"Plants are the eukaryotic organisms that constitute the kingdom Plantae. They are predominantly photosynthetic or came from photosynthetic ancestors, meaning that they obtain their energy from sunlight by using the green pigment chlorophyll in their chloroplasts to produce sugars from carbon dioxide and water. Over the course of time, some plants have evolved to be parasitic, meaning they take energy from other organisms. Except for glaucophytes, some green algae and a few red algae, most plants are multicellular."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Fr%C3%BChling_bl%C3%BChender_Kirschenbaum.jpg/330px-Fr%C3%BChling_bl%C3%BChender_Kirschenbaum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plant","wikidata":"Q756"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Haavoittuneita_Punaisen_ristin_sairaalassa_Tampereella_%2826901645371%29.jpg/500px-Haavoittuneita_Punaisen_ristin_sairaalassa_Tampereella_%2826901645371%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Haavoittuneita_Punaisen_ristin_sairaalassa_Tampereella_%2826901645371%29.jpg/1280px-Haavoittuneita_Punaisen_ristin_sairaalassa_Tampereella_%2826901645371%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Haavoittuneita_Punaisen_ristin_sairaalassa_Tampereella_%2826901645371%29.jpg/500px-Haavoittuneita_Punaisen_ristin_sairaalassa_Tampereella_%2826901645371%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Wounded patients at the Red Cross Hospital in Tampere, Finland during the 1918 Finnish Civil War","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHaavoittuneita_Punaisen_ristin_sairaalassa_Tampereella_(26901645371).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Micrasterias_radiata.jpg/500px-Micrasterias_radiata.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Micrasterias_radiata.jpg/500px-Micrasterias_radiata.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMicrasterias_radiata.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Climacium_dendroides_%E2%80%94_Flora_Batava_%E2%80%94_Volume_v9_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Climacium_dendroides_%E2%80%94_Flora_Batava_%E2%80%94_Volume_v9_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Climacium_dendroides_%E2%80%94_Flora_Batava_%E2%80%94_Volume_v9_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-Climacium_dendroides_%E2%80%94_Flora_Batava_%E2%80%94_Volume_v9_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Climacium_dendroides_%E2%80%94_Flora_Batava_%E2%80%94_Volume_v9_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Climacium_dendroides_%E2%80%94_Flora_Batava_%E2%80%94_Volume_v9_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AClimacium_dendroides_%E2%80%94_Flora_Batava_%E2%80%94_Volume_v9_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Glaucocystis_nostochinearum.jpg/330px-Glaucocystis_nostochinearum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Glaucocystis_nostochinearum.jpg/330px-Glaucocystis_nostochinearum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaig